          "source_quote": "ἐν τῷ ἐξεταστικῷ λόγῳ",
          "english_quote": "in the argument under examination",
          "issue": "This alternative in the lexical note reverses the adjective's direction: ἐξεταστικός characterizes discourse that examines or tests, not discourse that is itself undergoing examination. The main rendering “in the critical argument” is defensible in the examining or analytical sense, but this stated alternative is not adequately supported.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the unsupported alternative and explain the main rendering with “in the examining discussion” or “in the testing debate.” Retain the separately disclosed uncertainties concerning ὁμῶς, the writing and dispatch agents, and the genitive and participial attachments; those do not require a source-corruption block. Review the corrected note afresh.",
